Third-party material
--------------------

The chess pieces on the live-board pages are third-party artwork, shipped
as separate static files in `priv/static/pieces/` (one SVG sprite per set,
each beside its licence text) and loaded by URL, not compiled into the
code. The art keeps its own licence; the Elastic License 2.0 of this
project does not apply to it.

  - cburnett: "Cburnett" pieces by Colin M.L. Burnett, from Wikimedia
    Commons (File:Chess_klt45.svg and siblings). Offered by the author
    under GFDL, CC BY-SA 3.0, GPLv2+ and BSD 3-clause; used here under the
    BSD 3-clause licence. `priv/static/pieces/cburnett/LICENSE`.
  - chessnut: "Chessnut" pieces by Alexis Luengas
    (github.com/LexLuengas/chessnut-pieces), as packaged by lichess, under
    the Apache License 2.0. `priv/static/pieces/chessnut/LICENSE`.

The twelve files of each set were packed into one sprite (one <symbol> per
piece, ids prefixed so they cannot collide); the drawings are unchanged.

The flags beside federation codes are from flag-icons by Panayiotis
Lipiridis (github.com/lipis/flag-icons, the 4x3 set), under the MIT
License, shipped as separate static files in `priv/static/flags/` beside
the licence text (`priv/static/flags/LICENSE`) and loaded by URL, not
compiled into the code. Only the flags of FIDE's federations are included;
comments and whitespace were stripped from the files, the drawings are
unchanged. The table from FIDE's federation codes to the files is this
project's (`lib/openresults_web/flags.ex`).

One file there is not from flag-icons: `fide.svg`, drawn for players listed
under FIDE itself (code FID). It is "FIDE text on white" by Wikimedia
Commons user M5, dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0, set here in
the 4x3 box of the other flags (`priv/static/flags/LICENSE-fide.txt`). It
is the word FIDE in lettering, not FIDE's logo, which is not freely
licensed and is not shipped. "FIDE" is the name and a trademark of the
Federation Internationale des Echecs, used only to mark the federation a
player is listed under; no endorsement is implied.

The three games in `priv/live_sim` are public-domain games played before 1900
and in 1910 (the moves of a game are not protected), transcribed here for the
development simulator.

The move generator in `lib/openresults/chess.ex` is written for this project
and verified against the published perft node counts of the standard test
positions.
